  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 150 PM EDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nCurrently another warm day with highs expected to climb into the \n80's and 90's for most people in the Valley. A very weak boundary is \npushing thorugh the region, but that's more of a technical term as \nopposed to a change in weather. It will have little impact on our \nsensible weather, as warm temperatures will persist behind it for \nthe next few days due to a large mid/upper ridge across the region.\n\nGuidance has come in a couple of degrees lower on the dew points for \nthe upcoming week. So at this time it looks like we'll remain just a \nfew degrees below Heat Advisory criteria (105) for the week if the \nforecast verifies. But it for sure will be a very hot and muggy week \nwith highs expected to be in the 90 and 80's every day and dew \npoints right around the 70 degree mark. Very little chances of rain \neven with these warmer temperatures as the ridge remains overhead \nand squashes pretty much anything that looks to try and develop. \n\nLonger range models are showing a possible breakdown of the ridge in \nthe weekend or early next week as a couple of systems try and move \nthrough the United States fighting against the ridge.",
